{"cell": "ar25:L2", "arm": "flash", "iters_used": 4, "train_exact": 2, "train_n": 20, "heldout_exact": 2, "heldout_n": 20, "heldout_cell_acc": 0.9374, "baseline_nothing": 3, "baseline_lastdiff": 3, "tokens": [153322, 54907], "log": ["iter 1: content 0 chars, completion 16000 tok", "no code", "iter 2: content 0 chars, completion 16000 tok", "no code", "iter 3: content 0 chars, completion 16000 tok", "no code", "iter 4: content 4693 chars, completion 6907 tok", "iter 4: train exact 2/20"], "code": "# world_model.md\n#\n# Objects:\n#  - Background is 'b' (blue).\n#  - A vertical 3-column \"beam\" of 'S' (sky blue) spans rows 0..62; its left\n#    column is the beam position `s` (30, 33 or 36 in the recordings).\n#  - A right-hand border column (col 63) alternates between 'Y' (yellow) and\n#    'B' (black) in the upper region (rows 0..14) depending on the action.\n#  - Two \"stamp\" blocks (a charcoal 'c' block on the left and a black 'B'\n#    block on the right) appear in rows 18..29 when the beam is shifted right\n#    of its home position; they are a function of the beam position.\n#  - Static sprites in rows 42..52 (a 'B'/'W' creature on the left, a 'c'/'Y'\n#    crate on the right) and the bottom wall (row 63) are part of the level.\n#\n# Dynamics (per action):\n#  - LEFT  : beam moves left  by 3 columns (s -= 3), stamps update.\n#  - RIGHT : beam moves right by 3 columns (s += 3), stamps update.\n#  - DOWN  : beam moves right by 6 columns if not already at the far position,\n#            otherwise no change; upper border column becomes 'Y'.\n#  - UP    : beam does not move horizontally; stamps may still refresh.\n#  - SPACE : toggles a fixed pattern of 'W' (light-gray) pixels along the\n#            creature's columns and flips the upper border column.\n#  - UNDO  : restores previous board (not modelled -> no change).\n#  - MOUSE : ignored (no change).\n#\n# Goal: steer the 'S' beam so that the moving stamps align with the static\n# crates/sprites to complete the level (a beam-alignment puzzle).\n\ndef predict(board_lines, action):\n    H = 64\n    W = 64\n    grid = [list(row) for row in board_lines]\n\n    # find beam left column\n    s = 30\n    for c in range(W):\n        if grid[0][c] == 'S':\n            s = c\n            break\n\n    def clear_beam():\n        for r in range(0, 63):\n            for c in (30,33,36,39):\n                if grid[r][c] == 'S':\n                    grid[r][c] = 'b'\n\n    def draw_beam(sl):\n        for r in range(0, 63):\n            for c in (sl, sl+1, sl+2):\n                if 0 <= c < W:\n                    grid[r][c] = 'S'\n\n    # stamp templates keyed by beam left column\n    def stamps(sl):\n        # clear any old stamps in rows 18..29\n        for r in range(18, 30):\n            for c in range(0, 60):\n                if grid[r][c] in ('c','B','W'):\n                    grid[r][c] = 'b'\n        if sl >= 33:\n            # left charcoal stamp\n            for r in range(18, 21):\n                for c in range(sl-15, sl-7):\n                    if 0 <= c < W: grid[r][c] = 'c'\n            for r in range(21, 27):\n                for c in range(sl-15, sl-13):\n                    if 0 <= c < W: grid[r][c] = 'c'\n            for r in range(27, 30):\n                for c in range(sl-21, sl-13):\n                    if 0 <= c < W: grid[r][c] = 'c'\n            # right black stamp\n            for r in range(18, 21):\n                for c in range(sl+9, sl+18):\n                    if 0 <= c < W: grid[r][c] = 'B'\n            for r in range(21, 27):\n                for c in range(sl+15, sl+18):\n                    if 0 <= c < W: grid[r][c] = 'B'\n            for r in range(27, 30):\n                for c in range(sl+15, sl+24):\n                    if 0 <= c < W: grid[r][c] = 'B'\n\n    if action == 'LEFT':\n        ns = max(30, s - 3)\n        if ns == s:\n            return board_lines\n        clear_beam(); draw_beam(ns); stamps(ns)\n        for r in range(0, 15):\n            if grid[r][63] == 'Y': grid[r][63] = 'B'\n    elif action == 'RIGHT':\n        ns = min(36, s + 3)\n        if ns == s:\n            return board_lines\n        clear_beam(); draw_beam(ns); stamps(ns)\n        for r in range(0, 15):\n            if grid[r][63] == 'Y': grid[r][63] = 'B'\n    elif action == 'DOWN':\n        ns = min(36, s + 6)\n        if ns == s:\n            return board_lines\n        clear_beam(); draw_beam(ns); stamps(ns)\n        for r in range(0, 15):\n            grid[r][63] = 'Y'\n    elif action == 'UP':\n        stamps(s)\n        for r in range(0, 15):\n            if grid[r][63] == 'Y': grid[r][63] = 'B'\n    elif action == 'SPACE':\n        # toggle W pixels along creature columns and border\n        for r in range(1, 63, 3):\n            for c in (34, 37):\n                if grid[r][c] == 'W': grid[r][c] = 'b'\n                elif grid[r][c] == 'b': grid[r][c] = 'W'\n        for r in range(0, 15):\n            grid[r][63] = 'B' if grid[r][63] == 'Y' else 'Y'\n        # creature interior toggle\n        for r in (19, 22, 25, 28):\n            for c in (46, 49, 52, 55, 58):\n                if 0 <= c < W:\n                    grid[r][c] = 'W' if grid[r][c] == 'b' else 'b'\n    # UNDO / MOUSE -> no change\n\n    return [ ''.join(row) for row in grid ]\n"}
